<title>FRANCE: Axa-UAP has no comment on Suez-Lyonnaise.</title>
<headline>Axa-UAP has no comment on Suez-Lyonnaise.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Axa-UAP chairman Claude Bebear said on Wednesday he had no comment on the possibility of a merger between holding company Cie de Suez and utility group Lyonnaise des Eaux.</p>
<p>Axa-UAP holds 4.4 percent of Lyonnaise.</p>
<p>Asked by reporters if he planned to take any role in the matter, Bebear replied, &quot;No role.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;It is up to them to do what they want and we will take our decision as a consequence of that,&quot; he told reporters after a news conference at which Axa-UAP announced its results.</p>
<p>There has been increasing market talk that Lyonnaise and Suez will merge to create France's ninth biggest company in market value.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
